 "spec": "\u00a75.2.1.4 Message structure; \u00a713.3 label 'agora/broadcast/v1'; \u00a73.4 BroadcastKey; \u00a713.1.1",
 "notes": [
  "Fixed inputs named by a label are SHA-256(UTF-8(\"agora-test-vectors/\" || label)), truncated to the stated length.",
  "CBOR maps are encoded with RFC 8949 section 4.2.1 core deterministic key order and preferred integer widths. The spec does not require this order; it is one valid encoding, and receivers use the bytes as received.",
  "nonce is FIXED for the vector; the spec requires a fresh random 12-byte nonce per message.",
  "contentKey and channelID equal the key and channelID of the broadcast-key vector in jws.json.",
  "plaintext = encoded typed payload envelope {type, contentType, body, sig} of type urn:agora:type:BroadcastMessage, sig by the poster's did:key.",
  "broadcastPayload = nonce || AES-128-GCM(contentKey, nonce, plaintext, \"agora/broadcast/v1\" || channelToken). channelToken is derived from the broadcast admission key at keyEpoch 7, which signs the routing envelope."
